{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A man who sins</b> — [the vav] is parsed as <i>holem</i>: one who speaks smooth things to his fellow, perhaps he can deceive him." "<b>His feet</b> — joined with <b>a man who smooths</b>, like the matter of \"his hidden net will catch you,\" and the coming verse is a witness, meaning: because of sin a bad snare is set, or one bad snare."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "The reading בפשע ([the vav] parsed as holem) reflects the Hebrew text as given; the comment addresses a Masoretic parsing question about the word, likely the form יִפְשַׁע vs. a hypothetical יֹפְשַׁע."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:22.096568619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}